Z||000000||Monkeyman||05-04-2000||12:32 PM||||My wife just met Weird Al!  He had a performance at the Honeywell Center right here in Wabash, IN last night and stayed at the hotel my wife manages.  She was just talking to him a minute ago while I was on the phone with her.  He hollered, "Hi" to me.  Now I know a celebrity.  What a deal.  I could have met him, too if I could have gotten up to the motel in time.  SOB.  No car. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000001||bHooper||05-04-2000||01:29 PM||||Cool!  Isn't the Six Degrees of seperation a fascinating thing? (Just like the 6 degrees of Kevin Bacon)<P>I know for a fact that I am two people removed from the entire NHL... it works like this: my buddy knows Mark Messier's sister as well as Mark, Messier know's just about the entire list of who's who in the NHL.  Therefore I am 2 people removed from Gretzky, Gordie Howe and Maurice "The Rocket" Richard!<P>On the other hand, another friends father was a body guard for Benitto Mussillini!  So I am two people removed from Hitler, Hirhito, and Stallin!  Kinda sick when you look at it that way.<P>There are a lot of other combinations that are easy to figure out.<P>And yes, I am 3 people removed from Kevin Bacon!  A former boss met Bruce Willis and Demi Moore at a boxing match in Vegas!||||reg||1
Z||000002||GT Bastard||05-04-2000||05:11 PM||||Why are you happy, Monkey?!  You just found out that your wife is with a celebrity in a motel!  Anyhow, Wierd Al is cool.  He visited Sioux Falls a month or so ago and my girlfriend went to see him.  I guess it was pretty cool.||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||05-04-2000||06:35 PM||||Saw him at Kahunaville a few years ago. Name fits. It was fun, but I'll never go there again. the place sucks for a concert. not as bad a Stone Balloon, but bad enough.||||reg||1
